  "summary": "The `basic-ftp` FTP client library for Node.js contains a path traversal vulnerability (CWE-22) in versions prior to…",
  "details": "The `basic-ftp` FTP client library for Node.js contains a path traversal vulnerability (CWE-22) in versions prior to 5.2.0 in the `downloadToDir()` method. A malicious FTP server can send directory listings with filenames containing path traversal sequences (`../`) that cause files to be written outside the intended download directory. Version 5.2.0 patches the issue.",
